caption: Overview
setting-component: overview

France exists inside a divine compact with Niktul, the Blood God. On each new moon, France must provide Niktul with a large number of qualifying human sacrifices during a ritualized Blood Moon Hunt. In return, Niktul suppresses the supernatural conditions that make most of GATES Earth so dangerous.

While the Covenant is in force, France is held at approximately SPA 1, local mana is suppressed to Low Mana, spontaneous Gates do not open within the protected territory, and supernatural monsters are pushed away by a broad divine effect comparable in behavior to Avoid. This makes France unusually mundane, predictable, and safe by GATES Earth standards.

If France fails to meet Niktul’s required sacrifice quota by dawn, the protection ends. France immediately returns toward its natural GATES-Earth supernatural conditions: mana rises to High or Very High where appropriate, SPA returns to its natural level, spontaneous Gates can open again, and supernatural creatures are no longer repelled. The result is generally a disastrous remainder of the lunar month. At the next Blood Moon, France can satisfy Niktul again and restore the Covenant.
